# Secrets and local configuration. The .bak glob matters: `.env` on its own
# is an exact match, so a hand-made backup like .env.bak-prerename stays
# untracked only by luck and would be swept up by `git add -A`. Those copies
# carry AP_PASSWORD and BOA_PASSWORD in cleartext.
.env
.env.bak*

# Build outputs, anchored to the repo root. NOT a bare `dist/`: that pattern
# matches at any depth and would also exclude daemon/web/dist, whose
# placeholder index.html must be tracked or //go:embed fails to compile on a
# fresh clone.
#
# cache/ and dist/ are excluded deliberately, not just for tidiness: a built
# image is a derivative of Raspberry Pi OS and must not be redistributed from
# this repository. See docs/LICENSING.md.
/cache/
/work/
/dist/

# Compiled payload, produced by scripts/build-payload.sh
overlay/usr/local/bin/boad
# Compiled web interface. Everything here is a build product; only an empty
# marker is tracked, which is enough to satisfy //go:embed all:dist so a fresh
# clone compiles before the UI has been built.
daemon/web/dist/*
!daemon/web/dist/.gitkeep

node_modules/
.DS_Store

# memsearch plugin session memory. Contains conversation notes, including
# credentials that were discussed. Never commit.
.memsearch/

# Browser-automation scratch: screenshots and console logs written while
# checking the interface. Never part of the build.
.playwright-mcp/

# Claude Code local state: machine-specific settings, and worktrees/ which
# holds whole checkouts of this repo -- committing it would nest the tree
# inside itself.
#
# Written as .claude/* rather than .claude/, because git does not descend into
# an ignored DIRECTORY and the un-ignore below would never be reached. skills/
# is shared project tooling and belongs in the repository; everything else here
# is per-machine.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
